{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>As swallowing the holy.</b> An expression of swallowing — HaShem swallows and does not spare. That is to say: when they dismantle the Tabernacle and the Ark is exposed, if they let their eyes feast upon it they will die, as we find with the men of Bet Shemesh in the book of Samuel. So too it is implied that they distance themselves at the time the priests come to dismantle it, for it is written: ״ובא אהרן ובניו״ and the entire passage, ״וכלה אהרן ובניו לכסות״ etc., and afterward: ״יבואו בני קהת בגשתם אל הקדש הקדשים״ to dismantle its planks — then Aaron and his sons come and assign each man to his task and to his load, as is written above: ״ובא אהרן ובניו בנסוע המחנה״ etc. This is what is written immediately: <b>and they shall not come to see</b> etc. [As swallowing the holy — an expression of covering.] <b>Shlema, the passage of Bemidbar.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The bracketed remark appears to be an alternative gloss. The final line 'שלימא סדרא דפרשת במדבר' is a colophon marking the completion of the commentary on the parashah; 'שלימא' is Aramaic for 'it is completed.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:29.972808127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}